 "text": "Hi, how are you holding out? Try talking to her first instead of avoiding her. See if you can laugh together at the old stories, and then see if you can give her small project. Like tidying one room together, or finding a new container for her favorite kitchen habit. Then ask her if you can talk in the garden, so the environment isn't pushing its own story. She might, but at least you' together and not in the house. If she still goes too far, stop her and say we'll talk inside later. Tell her firmly that's none of her business, and that you'll help her with something small first, like tidying. Then stick to that, and don't let her go everywhere with it. It' worth a shot. After all, you want her to like the house, so finding a small project together is a win for both of you.",
